   "text": "This Project is my Christmas novella, [WORKING TITLE], written as [PEN NAME]. The house rules in the Project instructions apply to everything you do here.\n\nRead the Project files now and tell me, in one short list, what you found: voice source (skill, style sheet, or prose sample), banned-words block, trope stack, and any planning files (Brief, Codex, Outline, chapter prompts, progress tracker, Story State Ledger). Name anything missing that the next step needs. Do not summarize my files back to me and do not start planning.\n\nFile names we will use from here: [WORKING TITLE]_Brief.md, [WORKING TITLE]_Codex.md, [WORKING TITLE]_Outline.md, [WORKING TITLE]_Ch01_prompt.md (one per chapter), [WORKING TITLE]_progress.md, [WORKING TITLE]_StateLedger.md. Chapter drafts: [WORKING TITLE]_Ch01_draft.md, with _v2 for a re-draft.\n\nMy starting point: {{d:start|[new idea / partial draft / complete draft to revise]}}. Target: a complete novella draft by November 4, about [TARGET LENGTH] words, heat [HEAT]/5, [POV].\n\nConfirm you understand the roles in one line: you write, I edit and decide. Then wait for my next prompt.",
