   "label": "Fast lane A — The Brief in one pass (Worksheets 03 and 04, about 10 minutes)",
   "text": "Fast lane. Build my novella Brief in one pass. House rules apply.\n\nMy Worksheet 03 and 04 answers, rough is fine: {{x:ws34|[paste what you have; blank lines are allowed]}}.\nMy trope stack so far: wrapper [WRAPPER]; core tropes [CORE TROPES]; season does: [SEASON DOES].\nAbout [TARGET LENGTH] words, heat [HEAT]/5, [POV], draft by November 4. Starting point: {{d:start|[new idea / partial draft / revising a complete draft]}}.\n\nIf something essential is missing (my voice source, whether I am continuing an existing draft, or my heat level), ask for it in one short message first. Otherwise go.\n\nDeliver, in this order and nothing else:\n1. The 5 Core Elements in my words, sharpened: a specific subgenre; five tropes at most (one seasonal wrapper from the Holiday Trope Workbook list, two or three core tropes); a one-sentence hook; stakes with a character to root for, a nameable failure, and urgency that comes from the holiday itself; the emotional core for the reader.\n2. The Story Promise, one sentence: \"This is a [trope stack] romance about [the two leads] who are forced to [central situation] while hiding [secret or complication], leading to [promised emotional payoff].\"\n3. The five-point Costume Test: score out of 5, verdict (costume / halfway / real holiday book), the weakest unchecked point, and, if the score is 3 or below, one structural change that makes the season cause something, usually a deadline.\n4. A premise of one or two paragraphs that would survive as back-cover copy. No dates, no banned words, no new character names from the banned list.\nMark anything you had to assume with [CHECK] so I can correct it. Keep the whole Brief under one page and save it as [WORKING TITLE]_Brief.md.",
